From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LilSmokeOS <dev@lilsmoke.org>
Date: Thu, 1 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] direct: use POSIX union sigval for musl

DirectFB 1.7.7 uses sigval_t in the Linux/glibc Direct layer. That typedef
is not exposed by musl libc, while POSIX defines the actual sigqueue value
type as union sigval.

Use union sigval directly so the framebuffer-only DirectFB build works with
the LilSmokeOS musl toolchain.

Signed-off-by: LilSmokeOS <dev@lilsmoke.org>
---
 lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/system.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/system.c b/lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/system.c
index 0c4f4b2..7d78ed9 100644
--- a/lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/system.c
+++ b/lib/direct/os/linux/glibc/system.c
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@ direct_tgkill( int tgid, int tid, int sig )
 void
 direct_trap( const char *domain, int sig )
 {
-     sigval_t val;
+     union sigval val;
 
      if (direct_config->delay_trap_ms) {
           D_LOG( Direct_Trap, VERBOSE, "NOT RAISING signal %d from %s, waiting for %dms... attach gdb --pid=%d\n", sig, domain, direct_config->delay_trap_ms, getpid() );
-- 
2.39.2
